{"title":"GATE 2027-Topicwise Test-18 (EMI -2)","fileName":"058_GATE 2027-Topicwise Test-18 (EMI -2).html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2027 Online Test Series - Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A basic slide wire Potentiometer has a working battery voltage of 3 V with negligible internal resistance. The resistance of the slide wire is 400 &Omega; and its length is 200 cm. A 200 cm scale is placed along the slide wire. The slide wire has 1 mm scale divisions and it is possible to read up to 1/5 of a division. The instrument is standardized with 1.018 V standard cell with sliding contact at the 101.8 cm mark on scale. The working current and resistance of series rheostat are respectively</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>5 mA, 200 &Omega;</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>6 mA, 100 &Omega;</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>4 mA, 250 &Omega;</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>6.8 mA, 103 &Omega;</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/f6086892b61c75e97f4a4801fc384a5787c89099.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The no load current components of a current transformer are, magnetizing component is 120 A, core loss component is 30 A. The current transformer is 1000/5 A, then the percentage ratio error is _____ . (Assume secondary winding is purely resistive).</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>&ndash;2.9%</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>+2.9%</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>&ndash;1.4%</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>+1.4%</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/6bd4b643d317be7338303c38483a26c6f7fc4609.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":3,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A CRO probe has an impedance of 250 k&Omega; in parallel with a capacitance of &lsquo;<em>c</em>&rsquo; F. The probe is used to measure the voltage between <em>P </em>&amp; <em>Q </em>and observed as 3.82 V. Then the value of &lsquo;<em>C</em>&rsquo; will be ________ nF. (Answer upto two decimal places)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/dd13a4d7fb60c6f2af09f6a669a11bbd4830bc2b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"26","high":"27"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/ad7354e66e03b1d15570c58d68387c110a141140.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In the potentiometer circuit shown in figure balance is obtained.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a5b04c232ef8a337897200742a7b6a8689a04653.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The value of <em>R<sub>h </sub></em>is ______ &Omega;.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"200","high":"200"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/f5c82e1f9c09d477f118254c24be15a1e39635d7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/4671b5f1ebe67046ac41bbc5af603bbef0273dc2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>The impedances of a basic a.c bridge arm are:<br /><img src=\"/media/a1ff09124dd0abad4bbba81bed594b3db146b89f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /><br /><img src=\"/media/f67d82b4afa3bf5d4df04cb803990937edcdf1b8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>series with a capacitor of 4 &mu;F</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>parallel with a capacitor of 4 &mu;F</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>series with an inductor of 4 &mu;F</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>parallel with an inductor of 4 &mu;F</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/92c8cc4e8f42949d47122662a42d7d3ffda5b30d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/f19e1ed2674e20ac5dea11f91a1dfdb72a02c3a0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /><img src=\"/media/72f6c529a8d0e9886a0de8c98c81f6d95df71e1e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":6,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>In a Schering bridge, a sample of insulation forms the branch AB. The bridge is balanced using a supply at 50 Hz. The other arms of the bridge are found to be as follows:<br />branch BC: a loss free capacitor of 109 &mu;F,<br />branch CD: a non-inductive resistance of 309 &Omega; in parallel with a loss free capacitor of 0.5 &mu;F.<br />branch DA: a non&ldquo;inductive resistance of 100 &Omega;.<br />The capacitance, equivalent series resistance and loss factor of the capacitor are respectively</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>337 pF, 0.3256 M&Omega;, 0.0485</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>230 pF, 0.224 M&Omega;, 0.0485</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>337 pF, 0.4587 M&Omega;, 0.0485</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>337 pF, 0.523 M&Omega;, 0.06</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/e870f869e0cc24384f07dfc516274fb1e3644529.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/069cbff53e6177a5efad92e3b27de004b58a9463.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p> </p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/23d1a78dd597a9ed23709aa6ee2e8989ae583db1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/9676371d4971d6402032d472b2ed285df26ed110.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/729b8ac869e3f0e4a3223f874ccfde31eec279bd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/760000cab2dcce225a1e8c85b58f7f1344f792a6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/fb46568e8b36cd6d20796af6888d6a78403d3ce7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/0472d7e573261769436740086dbbde94abb9344f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>A dynamometer type of wattmeter is rated at 10 A and 100 V with full scale reading of 1000 watt. The inductance of the voltage circuit is 5 mH and its resistance is 3000 ohm. The error due to pressure coil inductance at rated VA with zero power factor load at 50 Hz will be</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>0.523 Watt</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>523 Watt</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>1.046 Watt</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>0.261 Watt</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/0214fb8d19ee747467dc04d42ca0e70bea300bf4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In the given circuit, the current through the galvanometer and voltage between terminal (a) and (b) will be</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/b4aa302b676a39d2fb3884d2b096e2302a4114b9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>0.027 mA, &ndash;0.5 volt</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>0.027 mA, + 0.5 volt</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>0.054 mA, &ndash;1 volt</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>0.054 mA, +1 volt</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/d2e05ced08d8c0ef575015c1854caff7acdce024.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":10,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A current transformer rated 200/20, has magnetizing current and loss component of exciting current as 10 A and 5 A respectively. The phase angle between secondary winding induced emf and current is 45&deg;. The phase angle error in degree at rated current is _______ degrees.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.9","high":"1.05"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/8e242e67a02a9f46f6746d50669b0ff2142a2cae.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":11,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/dc54ff7330ee3a7e1b9e1fe133582a885459c82f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.6","high":"0.7"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/5a3846a26a9153e05f1538da5d9e35d5aa077333.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/9e969bb9e2c555094ccff87e339e3eaf9db22cbf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":12,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/90b5bd7b02607418b2072a2ba71574de0fce02f0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>(a)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>(b)</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>(c)</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>(d)</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/fa823611d826ef8e0b446f600575c1936b5557aa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":13,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A cathode ray tube has anode voltage of 1800 V and parallel plate of length 1.8 cm each and 4 mm apart. The screen is 40 cm away from the centre of the plates. The amplifier gain before signal is applied to deflecting plate is 40, then input voltage for a deflection of 6 cm will be ______ V.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2.5","high":"3.5"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/cd8fa1b3250c848576c7034be61b21527908be9f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/63d28969bb1fe6901899d17c258cf397c4c9c932.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +1"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/a1c9db43c5107368e0277587394ce809196bd36b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>3.14</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>1.05</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>6.28</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>0.57</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/8a0803e47872aa177fda722fcc93fce0ad43331a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p><img src=\"/media/6ba15ae64288053e3a16753590fcb35dd173b785.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/40a1bc6b7800734bb9e695ed33b64c72fe986a5b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/4a06106257c3624cd360336792a94a3794654865.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/5e382dcf7a33fc9b04b3e4316336e340fa9c09d8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/caa2b35fb6df0bd644a0a0215f4f8a1355b9b5a0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/6e3fb1f2802722a3c819a7e65cf73764e19b9598.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/63a9f652e1a610e29e5eef59e00f7866eba4ce68.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A dc potentiometer is designed to measure upto 2 V with a slide wire of 1000 mm. A standard cell of emf 1.5 V obtains balance at 800 mm. A test cell is seen to obtain balance at 750 mm. Which of these statement(s) is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>Emf of test cell is 1.4062 volt</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>The sensitivity of potentiometer is 0.005 V/mm.</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>Potentiometer works on principle of potential divider.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>Potentiometer is not accurate.</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/c978fca2ad68a27b0a5592326a7534e7d387a4c7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"multi | Marks +2"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Two sinusoidal voltage signals of equal frequency are applied to the vertical and horizontal deflection plates of a CRO. The output observed on the screen is shown in the following figure.<br />The phase difference between applied signal is</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/0c9aeac21bf58d851064508a2af24e74328d4889.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>42.19&deg;</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>53.13&deg;</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>36.86&deg;</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>126.87&deg;</p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/1fd027928cd059ee0dbe7d367909192cad166a2a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:09.350Z"}